<Base title="Info" description="All the key information on Straussi Festival 2027: date, tickets, minimum age and rules.">
  {/* English version of pages/infos.astro. Keep both in sync. */}
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Info</h1>
    <p>The key information at a glance. More details in the <a href="/en/faq/">FAQ</a> and the <a href="/en/faq/#abc">Festival A to Z</a>.</p>
    <h2>Date and venue</h2>
    <p>Straussi Festival 2027 takes place on 11 and 12 June 2027 on the grounds of the Straussi student residences, Universitätsstraße 94, 70569 Stuttgart, Germany.</p>
    <p>There is no camping on site; Straussi Festival is a day festival.</p>
    <h2>Tickets</h2>
    <p>Tickets are sold through an external ticket shop (dein-ticket.shop). The “Buy tickets” button takes you there.</p>
    <p>Presale is on. There are <TicketLink>day tickets</TicketLink> for Friday or Saturday and <TicketLink>weekend tickets</TicketLink> for both days; all <TicketLink>ticket types</TicketLink> and prices are listed in the <TicketLink>ticket shop</TicketLink>.</p>
    <h2>Minimum age and ID</h2>
    <p><strong>Entry from 18 years only.</strong> Persons under 18 will not be admitted, not even when accompanied by parents or guardians.</p>
    <p>Please bring a valid official photo ID (ID card, passport or driving licence). No ID, no entry.</p>
    <h2>What can I bring, what not?</h2>
    <p>Not allowed are, among other things, weapons of any kind, pyrotechnics, bags larger than A4, glass containers of any kind, drones, illegal drugs and bulky items (please leave the sofa at home). You may not bring your own food or drinks either. The full list of prohibited items will be announced.</p>
    <p>Private photos and videos with your phone are allowed; professional photography and videography are not.</p>
    <h2>Food, drinks and payment</h2>
    <p>There is a wide range of food trucks and food stalls as well as alcoholic and non-alcoholic drinks. Free drinking water stations are spread across the whole site.</p>
    <p>Payment on the entire site is by card only; cash is not accepted.</p>
    <h2>On site</h2>
    <p>The info point, lost &amp; found and first aid are in the “Straussidreieck”, in the centre of the festival site.</p>
    <h2>Accessibility</h2>
    <p>The site is largely flat and therefore generally accessible. Some areas such as lawns or gravel paths may, however, be difficult for wheelchair users or people with reduced mobility. Details on accessible toilets, reserved areas and a contact person will be announced.</p>
    <h2>Awareness and safety</h2>
    <p>An awareness team is on duty on the festival site and can be approached in case of discrimination, harassment or other incidents. It is important to us to create a safe space free from racism, sexism, homophobia or any other form of discrimination. How to recognise the team, the code word and its exact location will be announced.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
